    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0416ac51",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "intended audience",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who are likely to engage with or share antisemitic content, particularly those who hold or are exposed to antisemitic stereotypes and conspiracy theories. The meme is designed to resonate with people who may identify with or support the 'Jews pretending to be white' trope, the 'Jewish world conspiracy' myth, or who are drawn to violent, hyperbolic rhetoric against Jewish people and the State of Israel. The use of the threatening dog as a visual metaphor and the explicit, hateful text are intended to provoke strong emotional reactions and potentially incite hatred or violence against Jewish communities. The target audience is not a specific demographic but rather a community of individuals who are receptive to and may be influenced by antisemitic narratives, including those who may be politically or ideologically aligned with far-right or extremist ideologies that promote antisemitism.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f6744fe4"
      },
